From ea5efa282302efdf0e6aaadbd2c4dd9a88d82571 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:56:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/32] sdhci: a PIO read waits for the end of the block on the
 Tegra 2

A PIO read took the buffer read enable bit of the present state as a
sign that a block was ready. The Tegra 2 sets it while the block is
still coming in: the driver read half a block of old data, and the rest
was left for the next read, so every read returned the data of the one
before. The self test of the AC100 eMMC then never got its reference
data, and the transfers were not checked after the bus timing changed.
The present state bit now counts only once the controller stopped
receiving; the buffer read ready status stays the main sign.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/busses/mmc/sdhci.cpp | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/mmc/sdhci.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/mmc/sdhci.cpp
index 9def0be33c..6d245caec4 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/mmc/sdhci.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/mmc/sdhci.cpp
@@ -1207,8 +1207,15 @@ SdhciBus::_TransferChunk(uint8 command, uint32 argument, uint32 blockCount,
 					status = B_IO_ERROR;
 					break;
 				}
-				if ((live & readyBit) != 0
-					|| (fRegisters->present_state.Bits() & bufferEnableBit) != 0) {
+				// The buffer enable bit of the present state counts only
+				// once the controller stopped receiving (read transfer
+				// active, bit 9, clear): the Tegra 2 sets it while a block
+				// is still coming in, and a block read then was half old
+				// data, the rest of the block left for the next read.
+				uint32 present = fRegisters->present_state.Bits();
+				bool bufferEnabled = (present & bufferEnableBit) != 0
+					&& (isWrite || (present & (1 << 9)) == 0);
+				if ((live & readyBit) != 0 || bufferEnabled) {
 					sPioReadyLive = live;
 					sPioReadyPresent = fRegisters->present_state.Bits();
 					break;
-- 
